TzD (task #42, TK 2026-11-13): a pointer slot off an 8-byte boundary is a
compile error.  __kernel_sockaddr_storage holds `void *__align` only for
its alignment, and the packed compat structs (compat_group_req and
friends) put it at offset 4.  An unsigned long gives the same size and
alignment and holds no pointer.  Nothing reads __align.
--- a/include/uapi/linux/socket.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/socket.h
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 				/* space to achieve desired size, */
 				/* _SS_MAXSIZE value minus size of ss_family */
 		};
-		void *__align; /* implementation specific desired alignment */
+		unsigned long __align; /* implementation specific desired alignment */
 	};
 };
 
